                <pb facs="0470" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9637: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-24T19:00:00+09:00">August 24, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 24—7:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>307. Embassy’s 297, August 23, 1 p.m. In conversation today with the Naval
                    Attaché, the Senior Aide to the Navy Minister stated that full evacuation of all
                    Japanese from Tsingtao is in process and will be completed within a few days. He
                    added that landing of Japanese forces will be avoided if at all possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
